board:0012 THE COMBAT BLOCKER: 7c1d passes 7e29 the HOST pointer, not the DI near-offset -- the fire
dispatch operated on garbage every tick so the spawn gate never opened.  asm 0x7c1d calls 7e29 with DI =
the firer's DGROUP near-offset; patch 244 re-points 7c1d's param_4 to the HOST pointer (g_mem+0x1c000+di)
for the object-relative body, but the 7e29 CALL still passes param_4, and 7e29 (patch 428) does di=(u16)
param_1 -> (u16)(host ptr) = a constant garbage near-offset (0x325c) NOT in the registry.  So all 1440
fire-attempts/run hit garbage [0xa8]!=0 -> gate never opens -> b1df-in-combat=4 -> no projectile -> no
combat.  FIX: pass 7e29 the near-offset (param_4 - (g_mem+0x1c000)).  This exposed the never-before-reached
SPAWN CASCADE (all host-ptr/int*-scaled base-loss, asm-verified, DS=DGROUP):
